# 2. Error Guessing on Flipkart Login Page

For error guessing, I considered mistakes that a normal user might make while entering login information.

| Test Case | Unusual Input                                         | Expected Behaviour                                                                  | Result / Observation                                                                           |
| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 1         | Very long email/mobile number                         | The system should reject invalid input and show a clear validation message.         | The input should not be accepted as a valid login detail.                                      |
| 2         | Password containing special characters such as `@#$%` | The system should accept it if it is a valid password format.                       | The system should process it normally and show an error only if the credentials are incorrect. |
| 3         | Both login fields left blank                          | The system should show a message asking the user to enter the required information. | Login should not proceed with blank fields.                                                    |
| 4         | Spaces before/after the entered value                 | The system should handle unnecessary spaces properly or clearly reject them.        | Incorrect credentials should not cause confusing behaviour.                                    |
| 5         | Invalid email/mobile format                           | The system should immediately show a useful validation message.                     | The user should understand what needs to be corrected.                                         |

**Conclusion:**
Error guessing is useful because it focuses on common user mistakes rather than only testing normal inputs. It helps identify validation and usability problems before they affect many users.

