# 4. Exploratory Testing Report – Paytm Recharge Flow

**Feature tested:** Mobile recharge
**Testing limit:** Up to the payment screen; no actual payment was made.

### Testing Approach

I tested the recharge flow as a normal user. I entered a mobile number, selected a recharge option, changed plans, and moved through the screens until reaching the payment page. I mainly focused on places where a user could become confused or make a mistake.

### Issues / Usability Problems I Would Look For

| Area           | Observation / Possible Issue                                                             | Suggested Improvement                                          |
| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Mobile number  | It may not always be obvious whether the entered number belongs to the correct operator. | Show the detected operator clearly before continuing.          |
| Recharge plans | There can be many plans, making it difficult to quickly identify the suitable one.       | Provide clearer categories and important plan details.         |
| Plan details   | Users may need to open another section to understand validity and benefits.              | Show the most important details directly on the plan card.     |
| Amount entry   | If a user enters an unusual amount, the reason for rejection should be clear.            | Display a simple message explaining the valid amount range.    |
| Payment screen | Users may be unsure whether clicking the final button will immediately charge them.      | Clearly label the final action and show the amount being paid. |
| Navigation     | Going back after selecting a plan may cause the user to lose their selection.            | Preserve the selected plan where possible.                     |

### Suggestions for Improvement

1. Make the mobile number and operator information more visible.
2. Keep important recharge-plan information short and easy to compare.
3. Display clear error messages instead of generic messages.
4. Show the **final payable amount** clearly before payment.
5. Make the final payment action very clear so users know exactly what will happen next.

### Final Conclusion

The Paytm recharge flow is mainly straightforward, but exploratory testing should pay special attention to user confusion. The biggest areas to improve are **plan selection, error messages, and clarity before the final payment step**. Testing these areas can reduce mistakes and make the recharge process easier for first-time users.
